00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:08.130
JAYANTH MYSORE: It
gives me great pleasure

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.180
to see all of you here.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.350
My name is Jayanth Mysore.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:14.160
I am the group product manager
responsible for enterprise

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.970
search products
within the G Suite.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:22.200
Today is an exciting day for
me, the product development,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.310
the sales, and marketing teams
that are behind this product.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:29.730
We are pleased to announce the
availability of Google Cloud

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.430
Search with third party
connectivity moving forward.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:33.960
Without further
ado, let me just get

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.292
started with what this product
is about, why they built it,

00:00:37.292 --> 00:00:39.250
and the benefits we hope
to bring to the market

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:40.291
through the same product.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.340
[APPLAUSE]

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:53.820
Motivating this product is
actually somewhat simple,

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.550
but it's also somewhat--

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.490
it tells us about the
times we live in, I guess.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:03.060
Enterprise search at this
point is a market space

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.140
that has been occupied by
so many companies, including

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:10.080
Google AdWords, Google
Search Appliance for more

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.580
than a decade, right?

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:15.300
But still, even today, when we
talk to leading analysts who

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.910
study how people spend time
at work, what we notice

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:22.080
is people waste upwards of 20%
of their time still looking

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.232
for information.

00:01:23.232 --> 00:01:25.690
There are many reasons for it,
we won't go into that today.

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:28.407
But I think most of us
intrinsically get it.

00:01:28.407 --> 00:01:30.240
Finding the content
that they're looking for

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.430
continues to be a
major challenge.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.560
It has been compounded
by the types of data,

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.470
by large amounts of log
data that people are trying

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.160
to analyze, things like that.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:41.100
But nevertheless,
the problem remains.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.140
On the other hand,
the importance

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:47.730
of information in the lives
of every single employee

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:49.900
has become
increasingly important.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:52.650
In fact, we come from
the school of thought

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:55.770
that splitting employees into
knowledge workers and everybody

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:57.510
else is fundamentally flawed.

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:59.610
There is a knowledge
worker strand

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:00.810
in every single employee.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:04.140
That's sort of how companies
these days should be thinking

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:07.440
about the workforce, anyway.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.930
Now, in this context, our
talk is pretty simple.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.980
What if we made finding
information as easy

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.510
as a metaphor that a lot of
us are very familiar with?

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.670
Just go to Google, right?

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:24.810
The convenience, the
intuitiveness, the scale,

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.840
the speed of finding
at Google we felt

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.900
should be made available
to every business.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:34.260
And we spent a fair bit of
time working with our system

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.057
integrator partners and
with a lot of customers

00:02:37.057 --> 00:02:38.640
who were kind enough
to let us come in

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:41.530
and observe how people
look for information,

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:45.720
and that has informed the
design of the product.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.450
So introducing
Google Cloud Search

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:50.610
with third party connectivity.

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:53.100
With this version of
Google Cloud Search,

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:56.550
businesses can now bring in
content from any location

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:00.960
on prem, on the Cloud, or
enterprise SAAS applications

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:05.940
through a rich set of
connectors and an indexing API,

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:07.950
all securely into an index.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.060
Let me just get
one level deeper,

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:11.880
this is a schematic
that walks you

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:14.550
through the parts of the
product, if you will.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:17.094
It would be rather
immature of me

00:03:17.094 --> 00:03:18.510
to call this an
architecture, it's

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:20.250
just a schematic at this point.

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:22.590
Going left to right, you
have the different types

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.110
of data sources as
I've been calling out,

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:29.070
on prem, public data
cloud services, and SAAS

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:30.610
applications.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:34.050
We are putting a lot of effort
to provide a scalable indexing

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:38.400
API and to bootstrap
the ecosystem provided

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.800
an SDK to make it easy
to write connectors

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.660
to all of these
different data sources,

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:45.810
and a handful of connectors
to get it all started.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:47.550
On the other end--

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:48.960
and this is a crucial point--

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.950
what we learned
through our users

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:52.710
studies and our
own market research

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:56.760
and observing how
businesses employ search is,

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:00.090
the moment you ask an
enterprise worker to leave

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:04.020
the application that defines
their work day, for a software

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:08.040
engineer it could be the
IDE, for a customer support

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:09.830
representative it could be--

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:12.240
I don't know, it
could be Salesforce

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.430
or it could be Service Now
or something like that--

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:16.470
the moment you tell them
to leave that surface,

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:18.839
you have actually created
enough of a distraction

00:04:18.839 --> 00:04:20.820
for them to not want to do it.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:24.060
So the key was to allow
search to happen in context.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:28.980
Hence, we provided both what we
call a query API and JavaScript

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:32.430
that allows you to create that
Google Ask search experience

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:33.660
exactly where you are.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.870
We call that the
embeddable search widget.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:41.340
And realizing the importance
of security to enterprises,

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:44.340
a lot of effort has gone into
the design of this product

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:48.750
in preserving the access
control models of every source

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:50.470
throughout the pipeline.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:50.970
Right?

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:55.650
So we have had very
gratifying stories told

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:58.260
from some of our early
customers wherein somebody

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:00.060
went an opened a
document and closed it

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.446
and [INAUDIBLE] changes, right?

00:05:01.446 --> 00:05:02.820
To us, it's not
a surprise, given

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.440
that's how Google
Search should work,

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.740
but we are very glad that
it makes people delighted.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.040
Right?

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.545
The other part of this
is that we have also

00:05:10.545 --> 00:05:13.920
put in a lot of effort into
understanding the importance

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:15.160
of people search.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:17.340
So we are creating
dedicated efforts

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:19.180
to make it easy to find people.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:21.660
So one feature that we're
working on from day one

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:24.760
is to give users of Cloud
Search immersive people

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.270
search experiences, as well.

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:27.820
Right?

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.910
I'm not stating that
two words that I

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.105
think I should state in
every conference these days,

00:05:32.105 --> 00:05:34.230
yes, this whole system is
based on machine learning

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:35.470
and artificial intelligence.

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:36.080
OK.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:39.636
So-- and because it's
search, we realize

00:05:39.636 --> 00:05:41.760
that search is an infrastructure
application that's

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:44.490
used across business
critical applications

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:47.040
and lines of business, we
put in a lot of thought

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:49.530
and made sure that this runs
on the same infrastructure

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:51.070
that powers Web Search.

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:54.730
So concerns around availability,
reliability, things like that

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:56.620
should be a non-issue, right?

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:00.280
And along the same lines,
we have studied the market

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:03.520
very closely and we have
come to conclude that Search

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:07.210
is a sufficiently sophisticated
application, that deploying

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:09.250
it would require nothing
more than thinking

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:12.310
about the number of
documents you want to index,

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:14.110
the number of queries
you expect to hit,

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:17.030
and make it easy for you, even
if the estimates went wrong.

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:19.810
We don't want you thinking
about how many VMs to spin up,

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:23.055
how many nodes to buy, how
many Linux boxes to run,

00:06:23.055 --> 00:06:23.930
and things like that.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:26.620
That's really not what setting
up a search application

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:27.770
should be about.

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:31.300
So a lot of thought has gone
into abstracting the service

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:34.000
to a model at which a buyer
can easily make a decision

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.820
and use without thinking
about it too much.

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:38.500
Right?

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:41.860
So all of that is
aboard the product.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:47.350
The part that I'm really
excited about is, from day one,

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:49.930
we have made sure that we
think about this product

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:52.780
as an ecosystem-lead offering.

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:56.410
What I mean by that
is, we within Google

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:59.200
are going to be focused
on what I would like

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:02.350
to think of as difficult
computer science problem

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:05.170
and exposing the
solutions and the ability

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:09.710
to access those solutions in
the form of APIs and SDKs.

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:11.950
But the actual
folks who are going

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:16.120
to bring this power to
businesses all over the world

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:19.690
are going to be our valued
ecosystem partners, both system

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:22.120
integrators and independent
software vendors.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.720
Right?

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:27.250
So the long list of connectors
creating custom solutions

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:30.370
for every business based on a
deep analysis of your business

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:34.990
workflows is all going to be
done by our esteemed ecosystem

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:35.950
partners.

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:37.840
And I feel extremely
fortunate to say

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:40.870
that even as we are
building the product,

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:46.040
we were lucky to get pretty much
the who's who in the ecosystem

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:48.130
when it comes to
such applications.

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:53.450
We have SADA, Onix, Accenture,
we have Perficient, TWT.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.740
We have businesses all around
the world partnering with us

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:59.680
even before we
launched the product.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:01.910
We have also had--

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:04.850
we've been very lucky working
with ISP vendors, as well.

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:07.930
And I'm very proud to say that
even today, as we announce

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:10.150
the product, we have
the product integrated

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:13.360
with Lumapps, which is an
enterprise-facing portal

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:16.930
provider servicing several
Fortune 1000 companies.

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:22.090
And without further ado, it
would be my pleasure and pride

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:26.279
to say that the first demo
of Cloud Search that most

00:08:26.279 --> 00:08:27.820
of the world will
see will in fact be

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:30.670
