want to find answers

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:25.210
rather than searching
for keywords.

00:13:25.210 --> 00:13:28.810
And so we want to provide
an experience that

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:31.360
assists the employee.

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:34.690
And so that's why we
focus on understanding

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:38.230
the natural language
of the user in order

00:13:38.230 --> 00:13:40.780
to interpret his request.

00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:44.000
We analyze the
behaviors of the users

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:47.090
with machine learning to
deliver a personalized search

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:52.420
experience, and we also assist
employees by suggesting stuff

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:56.410
that they may not even know
that they are looking for.

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:01.190
So now I will do a demo.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:03.680
So the use case I'm
going to present today

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:08.090
is about a picture database.

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:10.790
So you know we all have lots
of cooperate and marketing

00:14:10.790 --> 00:14:15.282
pictures, for
instance, from events.

00:14:15.282 --> 00:14:19.460
And wouldn't it be great
to be able to find pictures

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:23.720
based on their resolution,
colors, number of people,

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:26.330
or even emotions?

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:29.470
Let's see if we can do
something with Cloud Search.

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:36.600
So, if we can switch to--

00:14:39.301 --> 00:14:39.800
OK.

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:54.950
So this is a portal that
we published on Lumapps,

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:57.480
so you get all the
information for employees,

00:14:57.480 --> 00:15:00.260
so big announcements,
corporate content,

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:05.390
personalized
information, so it's very

00:15:05.390 --> 00:15:07.070
personalized for the employee.

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:10.070
And what we will be looking
at today during the demo

00:15:10.070 --> 00:15:14.840
is the search engine that's been
implemented with Cloud Search.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:20.000
So let's try to
find something fun.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:24.230
So I will switch to the
marketing images data

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:29.840
set that's been queried
live from Cloud Search.

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:31.580
And as you can see,
we can find here

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:34.810
results with a lot of metadata.

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:38.520
This metadata has been retrieved
using the Cloud Vision API,

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:41.390
and we'll explain it after.

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:44.240
And so is there
something funnier?

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:48.433
OK.

00:15:48.433 --> 00:15:49.220
Ta-da.

00:15:49.220 --> 00:15:53.480
You might know this guy, the
one with the orange glasses.

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:55.200
The thing is, he is
not really funny,

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:58.100
so I don't know why he
was picked up by GCS,

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:00.020
but, you know--

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:00.530
that's OK.

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:05.150
And as you can see,
on the right side

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:09.950
you have some facets that are
being provided by Cloud Search.

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:14.190
And so we can refine
the results dynamically.

00:16:14.190 --> 00:16:17.390
So let's say you want
to print something,

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:20.060
so I will pick up
the resolution.

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:24.020
I can see how many
numbers of results

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:27.050
have been reached
by Cloud Search.

00:16:27.050 --> 00:16:32.000
And if I want to say I want
only two people, for instance,

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:32.765
on the picture.

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:36.390
And that's it.

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:38.020
You get another picture.

00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:47.180
So I will explain
just after we assemble

00:16:47.180 --> 00:16:51.090
all the pieces of the Google
products to do this demo.

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:53.840
So just to finish
the demo, we also

00:16:53.840 --> 00:17:00.720
have a cross data
sources list of results.

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:04.220
So it's based on the
relevancy of the results.

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:07.250
And then you have
some custom data sets

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:09.480
that have been created
here [INAUDIBLE]..

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:12.980
So for all the posts
from our communities

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:16.010
are indexed and searched in GCS.

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:19.770
So here are the facets, are
the ones that we define.

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:22.800
So for instance the list of
communities that we have.

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:27.359
And so you can refine the
results using those facets.

00:17:27.359 --> 00:17:31.250
And, of course, you
have all the G suit data

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:35.810
sets out of the box, so
Email, Calendar, and Drive.

00:17:38.541 --> 00:17:39.040
OK.

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:41.260
So I will switch back
to the slide deck now.

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:47.140
[APPLAUSE]

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:55.890
So how we made that possible?

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:57.980
So we've uploaded
thousands of pictures

00:17:57.980 --> 00:18:01.420
on Google Cloud Storage,
and then we pipe them

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:04.130
to the Cloud Vision API.

00:18:04.130 --> 00:18:06.620
Using the Cloud Vision
API, we automatically

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:09.840
add information
about the pictures,

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:12.200
and then we uploaded
them on our system,

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:16.250
so we have categories,
colors, resolution,

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:18.830
entities in the pictures,
all the metadata

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:21.050
that you've seen
during the demo.

00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:24.230
Then, we ingest all
this information

00:18:24.230 --> 00:18:28.730
in Google Cloud Search using a
custom connector and the Index

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:29.960
API.

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:35.090
And then, finally, we use the
Query API from Cloud Search

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:38.360
to expose the results in our UI.

00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:42.260
And it wasn't it was not
even hard to implement.

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:46.010
I've been working with Google
technologies for the past eight

00:18:46.010 --> 00:18:48.200
years and I really
like these moments

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:50.630
when all the pieces
come together

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:53.240
and we can present a
use case like this.

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:54.260
Very, very exciting.

