00:24:09.419 --> 00:24:11.710
He saw me change something
and he's like, wait, go back

00:24:11.710 --> 00:24:12.920
and do that again.

00:24:12.920 --> 00:24:14.230
That already loaded?

00:24:14.230 --> 00:24:20.560
It was-- you know,
it's indexing content

00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:24.240
and being able to search
for it in one second.

00:24:24.240 --> 00:24:27.660
With the GSA, that
was 10 or 15 minutes.

00:24:27.660 --> 00:24:30.280
Number two, we write
a lot of connectors.

00:24:30.280 --> 00:24:33.137
We have to integrate with
a lot of content sources.

00:24:33.137 --> 00:24:34.720
Google has made this
very easy for us.

00:24:34.720 --> 00:24:39.550
They did not just throw us into
the ocean with an indexing API,

00:24:39.550 --> 00:24:41.590
they created a framework
that makes it easy

00:24:41.590 --> 00:24:44.770
for us to build connectors.

00:24:44.770 --> 00:24:46.600
The software
development kit takes

00:24:46.600 --> 00:24:49.690
care of a lot of the
indexing methodology.

00:24:49.690 --> 00:24:53.710
And I don't have to do all
the low-level plumbing.

00:24:53.710 --> 00:24:56.380
Third, the security.

00:24:56.380 --> 00:24:57.560
State-of-the-art.

00:24:57.560 --> 00:24:59.800
We have not run
across any systems

00:24:59.800 --> 00:25:03.370
that we have not been able
to emulate the security

00:25:03.370 --> 00:25:07.150
model in-cloud searches,
access control model.

00:25:07.150 --> 00:25:10.940
Lots of sophistication,
hierarchical inheritance,

00:25:10.940 --> 00:25:16.000
containerisation for modeling
things like sites and folders,

00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:21.790
complex identity mapping so I
can describe access permissions

00:25:21.790 --> 00:25:24.670
exactly as they are in
other identity providers,

00:25:24.670 --> 00:25:26.410
like Active Directory.

00:25:26.410 --> 00:25:27.590
Very impressive stuff.

00:25:27.590 --> 00:25:27.970
JAYANTH MYSORE: Great.

